  "solution": "Given:\n\ny + (1)/(y) = 11\n\nConcept used:\n\n1. (a - b)³ = a³ - 3ab(a - b) - b³\n\n2. (a + b)² = (a - b)² + 4ab\n\nCalculation: \n\ny + (1)/(y) = 11\n\n⇒ (y + (1)/(y))² = 11²\n\n⇒ (y - (1)/(y))² + 4 = 11²\n\n⇒ (y - (1)/(y))² = 121 - 4\n\n⇒ (y - (1)/(y))² = 117\n\n⇒ (y - (1)/(y)) = 3√{13} ....(1)\n\n⇒ (y - (1)/(y))³ = 117² over ³\n\n⇒ y³ - (1)/(y³⁾ - 3(y - frac {1}{y}) = 117² over ³\n\n⇒ y³ - (1)/(y³⁾ - 3 × {3√{13}} = (3√{13})³\n\n⇒ y³ - (1)/(y³⁾ = 351√{13} + 9√{13}\n\n⇒ y³ - (1)/(y³⁾ = 360√{13}\n\n∴ The value of y³ - (1)/(y³⁾ is 360√{13}.\n\n [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/c76c13ba2d2ab46b47f8a931ae621dac081a0cb266b142dc23f58659fac4a466.png] **__Alternate Method__** If y + 1/y = p, then\n\ny - 1/y = √(p² - 4) = q and y³ - 1/y³ = q³ + 3q\n\nNow, y + 1/y = 11\n\ny - 1/y = √(11² - 4) = √117 = 3√13\n\ny3 - 1/y3 = (3√13)³ + 3 × 3√13\n\n⇒ 27 × 13√13 + 9√13\n\n⇒ 351√13 + 9√13 = 360√13\n\n**∴ y3 - 1/y3 = 360√13**\n\n1a0:T1914,\n&l",
